// this file makes that §5 leaves open.
//
// Every mutation in the system arrives here. Agents never read or write the project file
// directly (§5), so this service is the whole of what can be done to a song.
//
// Three rules shape the file, all from ADR 0006:
//
//   1. Every mutating RPC returns ToolResult. One contract, not sixteen copies of one.
//      Reads return what they read; `valid` and `patch` mean nothing for them.
//   2. Requests embed escribass.song.v1 entity messages wherever a whole entity is meant.
//      A hand-written NoteSpec mirroring Note is a second representation of song state
//      (CLAUDE.md #1) under another name, and it stops matching the first time a field is
//      added to song.proto.
//   3. Errors are Violation, the same path/rule/message shape core already returns. An
//      invalid call comes back as ToolResult.valid = false, never as a transport failure:
//      §6's retry loop has to be able to see it.
